        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>These full-length orthotic insoles are built for people who need reliable support without overly rigid correction. The design focuses on <strong>moderate pronation control</strong>, making them suitable for everyday walking, standing, work shifts, and light-to-moderate activity rather than extreme athletic correction. The arch support follows a clinically designed contour that helps stabilize the foot and ankle, reducing excess movement that often contributes to plantar fasciitis, heel pain, and general foot strain. Unlike flat cushioning inserts, the structured arch works to distribute pressure more evenly across the foot, which can noticeably reduce stress on the heel and plantar fascia over time. Cushioning is where these insoles quietly stand out. A <strong>dual-layer system</strong> combines firm support with softer top-layer padding, offering comfort without collapsing under body weight. The heel area is especially well-padded, absorbing impact with each step and helping reduce fatigue during long periods of standing or walking. Fit is straightforward and frustration-free. Since they’re sized by shoe rather than trimmed, the insoles sit cleanly inside athletic shoes, walking shoes, work footwear, and many casual styles without shifting or bunching. That makes them practical for people who rotate shoes throughout the week.</p>",
